Product Search
Key details
Priority


Highest
Description

Allow customers to find products by typing a product name or keyword, including partial matches and products that are out of stock.
Why are we carrying this out?
Customers should be able to find what they want without knowing the exact product name, so they can browse and buy more easily.
Work to complete
Add a product search that accepts a product name or keyword.
Match products on partial terms, for example "headphone" returning "headphones".
Show the product name, description and image for each result.
Show accurate availability for each result, including "Out of Stock".
Show a clear message when no products match the search term.
Additional Information
Related: KAN-6 (Epic, "TC5- Browse products") covers the wider browsing area and has no description yet.
Constraint (business): the system must detect both keywords and product names.
Constraint (business): availability information must be accurate.
Assumption (high risk): all products have accurate keywords. Products that are not tagged correctly will not be found.
Assumption (low risk): searches with irrelevant keywords show the no-results message.
Source: tickets/Day 1 search browsing.md.
Acceptance Criteria
Given a customer searches by product name or keyword, when matching products exist, then those products are shown with name, description and image.
Given a customer searches with a term that matches no products, when results are returned, then a clear message is shown.
Given a matching product is out of stock, when it appears in the results, then it is shown as unavailable.
Given a customer enters a partial term such as "headphone", when results are returned, then all related products are shown.